{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:42:48.979633Z","id":"8f4d6db162f75592e06f5d2207573cecdcc41f1084020c1317b9766889c6e5f6","body":{"detail":"scripts/test-quickstart.sh runs the line verbatim with no network: parse_pathbase_ref (crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:415, extract_triple) requires /<owner>/<repo>/graphs/<uuid> and fails on 'path-pr-42'. The rest of the flow passes in that script with the URL path share prints. Fix the example to a real graph URL (or make the CLI resolve slugs), then drop this concern.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":238},"end":{"line":238},"content_hash":"5b937b262fd07c05376b8b98598cc3fe97c5574cbb9f032785a942cf1c08dcbe"},"suggested_fix":"Use a URL of the form https://pathbase.dev/u/<owner>/repos/<repo>/graphs/<uuid> in site/index.md, or teach parse_pathbase_ref to resolve a slug","summary":"The quick start's resume URL cannot resolve: pathbase.dev/alex/pathstash/path-pr-42 ends in a slug, and the CLI refuses anything but a graph UUID before making a request","tags":["quickstart","site-claim","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.006456Z","id":"e4729b539d138608cc2876c3dd3bf9c5e6cf6d014b79e719addeb2a5a868eeb2","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0 (LICENSE, workspace license). Versioned: kind URIs agent-coding-session/v1.0.0 and v1.1.0 ship side by side; cmd_validate::legacy_kind_warns_once_per_path_and_still_validates and cross_harness_matrix::no_source_spells_the_superseded_kind_outside_the_legacy_constant; every golden's validate@<set>.snap is valid.","kind":"pass","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"b45e177f9b57ed4d371be3b7ed78be444c464c09d3523fb483cad12d35ed5d85"},"summary":"Claim: open, versioned format for coding-agent sessions — backed","tags":["claim:open-versioned-format","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.006607Z","id":"1c66e6477a486b13b168577c3081356cd5fd4f9bcd18834e7d12e42a8ca42804","body":{"detail":"Parse: ir@/document@/validate@ snapshots for all 7 harnesses. Project: all 49 pairs pinned (projection@, round_trip@), but projections into opencode, gemini and cursor carry losses no known-defect declares, and writers invent values the source never had (model_provider \"openai\", permissionMode \"default\", cli_version \"0.0.0-projected\"; docs/model findings of kind invented_value). Missing: declared or fixed losses for those three targets, and synthesized values marked as such.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"da34c22e710da21cc75ff961d995a2731013db2e92651c3b74a521ce6e4be03f"},"summary":"Claim: parse any agent's session in, project it out to any supported harness — partly backed","tags":["claim:parse-in-project-out","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.006679Z","id":"0222a64753a4d659626f052cc10eacb2008293095a723c32937bfc50468027bc","body":{"detail":"One schema is real (schema/toolpath.schema.json; validate@ for every harness). But only path query is exercised as a cross-harness tool, and its tests (crates/path-cli/tests/query.rs) seed claude and git-PR documents, not sessions from all seven harnesses.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":14},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"c53419b87615c3b1ad79d7703056337341b60bfe881851e1bcd33668c62aaa13"},"summary":"Claim: build your tools once for all of them — partly backed","tags":["claim:build-tools-once","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.006743Z","id":"a0325c33cde03d75fb4590a84a6546b369a49aa86ba743533ba738b473872313","body":{"detail":"Observed twice in this work: gemini-cli 0.47 moved to session-*.jsonl (pr/19, 635f8dc) and Cursor 3.24 moved its composer index to a table (pr/20, e0415cd); the format notes under docs/agents/formats record each harness's layout as reverse-engineered, not documented.","kind":"pass","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":70},"end":{"line":71},"content_hash":"3a61b8d44faeae92fcc248e4e0ed5f9b4b33c3a96e80ecd00e9307d9963a2778"},"summary":"Claim: harness logs are undocumented and change between releases — backed","tags":["claim:where-sessions-live","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.006798Z","id":"f6ed7ce894631324bc235de1e4dbca223904a22edd9dca03f30cd122bc49c681","body":{"detail":"The CLI's harness operations are p import/derive (parse), p export (project) and resume (projection + exec); crates/path-cli/tests/resume.rs covers resume for all six writable harnesses (file_input_explicit_*_projects_and_records_exec).","kind":"pass","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":83},"content_hash":"5a0f6dd8cd6431f042cde85f00aade26a69c997505395341fd6124f5fb056890"},"summary":"Claim: everything is parse in, project out, or resume — backed as a description","tags":["claim:three-moves","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.006866Z","id":"a8d25bbeeae04a39d36910805232b9c39b0e54ff0b29ecf05e344107d8320f33","body":{"detail":"No harness reader sets meta.intent: toolpath-convo's derive never writes it, so an agent-coding-session document has no intent; only git/github derivation and p track set it. dead ends and usage are carried (toolpath query dead_ends tests; token_usage on steps).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":95},"content_hash":"80969c402ca8df06df680318b862c4267215ae7ec7202472817a72cce09cce5e"},"summary":"Claim (FIG_002): a document carries meta.intent (why) — not for agent sessions","tags":["claim:fig2-intent","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.006927Z","id":"ec6310d10c7a7ee2feb0850049fd912df7b19631a5a9db8bcd25f13e027a0c00","body":{"detail":"ir@/document@/validate@ snapshots pin the document for every golden; query: crates/path-cli/tests/query.rs; share: crates/path-cli/tests/integration.rs share_records_manifest_so_sync_skips, share_uploads_cached_doc_when_source_unchanged.","kind":"pass","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":107},"end":{"line":108},"content_hash":"ee27986f17447d2fc837ae4e5aa95734cff5e7b8bc213a641d0f5e52fead7830"},"summary":"Claim: a parsed session is a stable document you can keep, query and share — backed","tags":["claim:parse-in-stable","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.006981Z","id":"ace4fd84f4ed8aa7d6d4ac5a6825ea5ba3bd1d1a3bdfad27d973e418ebed918d","body":{"detail":"Every pair is projected and pinned (projection@<set>@<harness>, 54 snapshots), and writer@<harness> pins each writer alone (86c325b). Gains: writers add values the source never had and readers read them back as real (round_trip@ gained lists; docs/model invented_value findings).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":111},"content_hash":"d95abe36f5a67b2a3ec7e34cb013f74bb24acc2daaf42f1a9073070f6b279f62"},"summary":"Claim: project out to any writable harness — partly backed","tags":["claim:project-out-any-writable","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.007042Z","id":"e340049bed521c2223fdc7d3f255f3dd90086a1769ed1db5df6ac16978d08121","body":{"detail":"Live resume matrix (scratch review/resume-matrix-v2..v5, not committed): Claude Code, Codex, pi and Copilot load and answer in every combination; opencode answers from 3 of 4 sources (pi -> opencode gets no reply); gemini untested (key refused); Cursor lists the session but the transcript is not read back. Committed: crates/toolpath-harness-mock covers Claude Code as a target only (8f6837e) and finds opencode -> claude reaching 2 of 22 entries.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":112},"end":{"line":113},"content_hash":"df7ab5eb8d65e8d8432c1e91820126df8e9e8e2ebb0489359fb67eccd7285e9c"},"summary":"Claim: start in one agent, continue in another — 19 of 28 resume cells shown","tags":["claim:resume-handoff","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.007110Z","id":"037514d54440e40834240324421d479d76fcebdc34d90b31a92632ed0274459b","body":{"detail":"shed@<set>.snap lists every dropped key path with an example value; round_trip@<set>@<harness>.snap lists lost and gained key paths for all 54 pairs. Note: gains are reported but not judged.","kind":"pass","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":113},"end":{"line":114},"content_hash":"243775531f78b5e9fbd614e704141606ad6b2e310b4dada80fadeed2f8dd8211"},"summary":"Claim: what a harness cannot hold is dropped and the shed reports say what — backed","tags":["claim:drops-are-reported","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.007166Z","id":"57513f566111d5e0bfdc6187d4d35c975eb5a97f589460fd92054674b9e859d1","body":{"detail":"Every harness's document validates against the one schema (validate@ for all 9 sets). No test runs a consumer (query, render, share) over documents from all seven harnesses.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":118},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"e5cc2a765172a43cab6d1c078129eb6e18b80af312bdf99384b1500612ef0c6b"},"summary":"Claim: build against the format, it works with sessions from every harness — partly backed","tags":["claim:one-schema","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.007224Z","id":"631b79eaaa9ce8c46a8511a80912553b61847c4cf3461dbbb8cb6cf369740f87","body":{"detail":"Forward-looking. Projection code for several harnesses lives in path-cli (crates/path-cli/src/projection/*), so adding a harness is a parser plus a projector plus path-cli wiring, not one parser.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"2fa47f2b686f06e623661a911620c0ff5b67db5386e592fffc494a31b39265a6"},"summary":"Claim: one new parser brings the next agent into every tool — not tested","tags":["claim:next-agent-one-parser","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.007283Z","id":"eeb4f9c4f1f746349bf089cab18cca1bf44e63c8ab32097a81bca895a575c3d8","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/tests/query.rs runs filters over a seeded cache (one agent-coding-session doc and one git-PR doc) with $HOME sandboxed empty; no test syncs sessions from all seven harnesses and queries them, and the home page's exact output-tokens filter is not run anywhere.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":125},"end":{"line":125},"content_hash":"892798a3ce06d7385f2465f241dd3467aa043b2a411e06a3fa4768600b591dfc"},"summary":"Claim: path query runs one jq filter across every session on the machine — not tested as stated","tags":["claim:query-every-session","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.007336Z","id":"e8798c3bc330491884c6a9912a51258c1d831de4f8640da6f7087e691955d56b","body":{"detail":"Projection pinned (projection@claude@codex, round_trip@claude@codex; known defect claude-to-codex-caller-cwd) and resume.rs file_input_explicit_codex_projects_and_records_exec; that Codex answers from the history is shown only in the scratch resume matrix. A round trip drops codex's sandbox policy (shed@codex).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":130},"end":{"line":132},"content_hash":"705159437612d7a3bddae31b899a621f0fe089161938147c16ad20a132d1f24d"},"summary":"Claim: path resume --harness codex moves a Claude Code session into Codex — shown live, not committed","tags":["claim:resume-anywhere","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.007388Z","id":"5e842b71fd6c1bb3d75631e728b9786a118b201e2637310e184dc32808c17ed2","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs tests: first_sync_ingests_then_second_is_unchanged, changed_session_is_rederived, rotated_session_resyncs_under_its_head_id, copilot_syncs_and_scopes_via_memoized_peek, evicted_cache_entry_rematerializes_on_next_sync. Kinds are versioned so cached documents stay valid (see open-versioned-format).","kind":"pass","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":137},"content_hash":"db0eb666872730c8890d8eb4506dc41d5b10e813e05857d71f91376384827b78"},"summary":"Claim: path p cache sync keeps every session incrementally in one format — backed","tags":["claim:archive-search","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.007441Z","id":"1555fcd2b2ab7e656d62eeccee57e14e2313c3ffbc8a6445c33721f0151684ae","body":{"detail":"Share/store/stats/read-back are pinned in pathbase-goldens (stored@, stats@, ir_back@, losses@) and toolpath's share tests. Resuming from a Pathbase URL: only cmd_resume::resolve_input_url_dispatches_to_pathbase_fetch (dispatch), no end-to-end test.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":142},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"020584061edffec370520ed5d3c6a18dbc110b0b46fe7a7a6858155a5fcd405f"},"summary":"Claim: Pathbase stores, shares and resumes sessions — share pinned, resume not","tags":["claim:pathbase-stores-shares-resumes","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/index.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:20:23.007502Z","id":"2d3ecf7cbe2da94092327af340ac39085b229c2ec8312755728e748ab8c83c38","body":{"detail":"A Pathbase product behaviour; nothing in this repo tests the rendered view, and agent-session documents carry no meta.intent (see fig2-intent).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:86c325b","span":{"start":{"line":143},"end":{"line":144},"content_hash":"86400ab55f42ab36cd2fa8b1d267da5187f08493d36b14b8c1e01ece74130280"},"summary":"Claim: link a session from a PR and reviewers see what was asked, tried, rejected — not tested here","tags":["claim:pr-reviewers-see","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
